course: dictionary
lesson: 14007
title: Lunatic: a word with two faces
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Lunatic» is an informal word for someone who behaves in a wild, silly or dangerous way. «He drives like a lunatic» means he drives recklessly. «That is a lunatic idea!» means the idea is very silly or crazy. Use the clues around the word to find which meaning fits.
explain: Some words change over time. In old history books you may find «lunatic asylum», an old name for a hospital for people with mental illness. Today we do not use «lunatic» for people who are ill, because it is hurtful. We say «mental illness» or «psychiatric hospital» instead.
explain: Words tell us a story about the past. «Lunatic» comes from the Latin word «luna», which means moon. People once wrongly believed the moon made people mad. We now know that is not true, which is one reason the word has changed.
fact: «Lunatic» is informal when it means a wild, silly or dangerous person.
fact: As an adjective, «lunatic» means very silly or crazy, as in «a lunatic idea».
fact: The old use of «lunatic» for people with serious mental illness is now offensive.
fact: Today we say «mental illness» and «psychiatric hospital» instead.
fact: «Lunatic» comes from the Latin «luna», meaning moon.
exercise: «He drives like a lunatic on the icy road.» What does lunatic mean here? | Very tired and slow | A doctor who helps sick people | *Wild, reckless and dangerous | Calm and careful
exercise: Mia says, «That is a lunatic idea!» What does lunatic mean? | Very clever and useful | A kind and gentle idea | *Very silly or crazy | Very old and worn
exercise: An old history book says «lunatic asylum». Why don't we use lunatic about sick people today? | *It is hurtful, so we say mental illness instead | It means very clean | It is a rude word for a dog | It is too long to spell
test: «Her lunatic plan to climb the tallest tree made everyone laugh.» What does lunatic mean? | *Silly and crazy | Very quiet | Sleepy and calm | Hungry
test: Which is the kind, modern way to talk about a serious illness of the mind? | *Mental illness | Wild drive | Lunatic | Silly idea
exam: Which sentence should we NOT say today, because it is hurtful? | *«My aunt has a serious mental illness, so she is a lunatic.» | «The swimming pool was closed on Monday.» | «The sea was calm and blue.» | «That plan is a lunatic idea, so let's change it.»
